# Test: ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall config validate agrees with daemon start, while validate without --plugin accepts.
# Question: does `ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall config validate` on a file
#           setting only `interface backend vpp` refuse it with the same words
#           as `ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall start`, naming `--plugin
#           ze.flowspec-firewall` and `set firewall backend vpp`, while
#           `ze config validate` without `--plugin` accepts the same file?
#           A unit test sets the process record manually; only invoking the
#           real `ze` binary proves `zeDispatch` records global `--plugin`
#           flags ahead of both `config validate` and `start`.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-3, AC-18 (Q-2) -- global
#            `--plugin` arguments are honored by `ze config validate` and
#            `ze start` with identical data-plane refusal wording, and omitted
#            `--plugin` leaves the file valid.
# PREVENTS: `ze config validate` dropping global `--plugin` flags and reporting
#           valid for a file that `ze --plugin ... start` refuses.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_vpp:state=present

tmpfs=vpp-only.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall config validate vpp-only.conf:exit=1:timeout=20s
expect=stdout:contains=--plugin ze.flowspec-firewall
expect=stdout:contains=set firewall backend vpp
expect=stdout:contains=start without --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate vpp-only.conf:exit=0:timeout=20s
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall start vpp-only.conf:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: load config:
expect=stderr:contains=--plugin ze.flowspec-firewall
expect=stderr:contains=set firewall backend vpp
expect=stderr:contains=start without --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall
reject=stderr:contains=interface backend loaded
